Sval: SessionStore completes no restore its window's close abandoned

Closing a window runs onClose, which resets the restoring state of each tab
still restoring and moves the restore queue on. The load each of those tabs
was waiting for still settles afterwards, and _restoreTabContentComplete then
finds the tab in the closed window's gBrowser, asks _resetLocalTabRestoringState
to reset it again, and logs "Given tab is not restoring." Sval restores a
workspace's tabs through setTabState whenever a window opens on one, so closing
that window before its tabs finish loading logs the error. A tab whose
restoring state is gone has nothing left to complete.

diff --git a/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs b/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
index 6253d6590a..676f548811 100644
--- a/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
@@ -8558,6 +8558,10 @@ var SessionStoreInternal = {
     if (!tab) {
       return;
     }
+    // The restore was abandoned while it loaded, as when its window closes.
+    if (!TAB_STATE_FOR_BROWSER.has(browser)) {
+      return;
+    }
     // Restore search mode and its search string in userTypedValue, if
     // appropriate.
     let cacheState = lazy.TabStateCache.get(browser.permanentKey);
